#
# Counter-example for math:ConditionedAssertionShape (Rule P8): a math:ConditionalProbability
# that names NO math:conditionalOn — the B in P(A | B) is left implicit — so that property's
# sh:minCount 1 fires — shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent (math:UnconditionedAssertion).
# Single violation: math:ConditionalProbability is a math:MathematicalObject subclass carrying
# no other SHACL target shape, and this node trips no other math: gate — EXACTLY ONE finding.
# Back-reference: math:ConditionalProbability / math:UnconditionedAssertion (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecConditionalProbabilityUnconditionedBad).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:unconditionedProbability a math:ConditionalProbability .
